# Planted bugs for the one-transaction design. Each one must make its property fail.
run fv-tlc TransactionalOutbox.tla OneTransaction.cfg WitnessDuplicateDelivery.cfg
properties NoEventWithoutCommit AtMostOnceApplied EventuallyApplied
file TransactionalOutbox.tla

mutation the one-transaction write marks the outbox row without committing the business row
detects NoEventWithoutCommit
-     /\ committed' = TRUE /\ outboxWritten' = TRUE
+     /\ committed' = committed /\ outboxWritten' = TRUE

mutation the consumer applies the effect without checking its dedup key
detects AtMostOnceApplied
-     /\ applied' = IF ConsumerDedup /\ applied >= 1 THEN applied ELSE applied + 1
+     /\ applied' = applied + 1

mutation a crash after the relay publishes gives up instead of retrying
detects EventuallyApplied
-     ELSE IF ~outboxMarked THEN "outbox_written_pending_relay"
+     ELSE IF ~outboxMarked THEN "done"

harmless a comment on the resume point
- \* The point the process resumes at, decided by what it wrote durably.
+ \* The point the process resumes at, decided only by what it wrote durably.
